picoCTF{wh47_h47h_90d_w20u9h7}
 ──────
  ### Step 1: Understand the Standard Morse Timing Rules
  Morse code relies on relative time units (T):

  • Dot (.): 1 unit of sound.
  • Dash (-): 3 units of sound (3 × longer than a dot).
  • Gap between parts of the same letter: 1 unit of silence.
  • Gap between letters: 3 units of silence.
  • Gap between words: 7 units of silence.
  ──────
  ### Step 2: Visualize the Audio in Audacity
  The most accurate manual way is by viewing the beeps visually:
  1. Open the file in Audacity:
    audacity morse_chal.wav &
  2. Switch to Spectrogram View:
      • Click the drop-down menu next to the track name (on the left panel).
      • Choose Spectrogram.
  3. Zoom in (Ctrl + 1):
      • You will see bright blocks at a specific audio frequency:
          • Short box → .
          • Long box (3 × length) → -
          • Medium silence gap → space between letters (add a space in your notes)
          • Long silence gap → word boundary (add / in your notes)
  ──────
  ### Alternative: Generate a Spectrogram Image via Terminal

  If you prefer viewing an image directly without opening Audacity, use sox:

    # Install sox if needed: sudo apt install sox
    sox morse_chal.wav -n spectrogram -o spec.png
    xdg-open spec.png
  ──────
  ### Step 3: Translate the Dots and Dashes to Letters

  Once you transcribe the sequences into dots and dashes, look up each letter:

  #### Letters (A–Z)

          Char        | Morse              |        Char        | Morse             |       Char        | Morse             |       Char        | Morse
  --------------------|--------------------|--------------------|-------------------|-------------------|-------------------|-------------------|-------------------
           A          | .-                 |         H          | ....              |         O         | ---               |         V         | ...-
           B          | -...               |         I          | ..                |         P         | .--.              |         W         | .--
           C          | -.-.               |         J          | .---              |         Q         | --.-              |         X         | -..-
           D          | -..                |         K          | -.-               |         R         | .-.               |         Y         | -.--
           E          | .                  |         L          | .-..              |         S         | ...               |         Z         | --..
           F          | ..-.               |         M          | --                |         T         | -                 |                   |
           G          | --.                |         N          | -.                |         U         | ..-               |                   |

  #### Numbers (0–9)

                    Num                   | Morse                                  |                  Num                   | Morse
  ----------------------------------------|----------------------------------------|----------------------------------------|---------------------------------------
                     1                    | .----                                  |                   6                    | -....
                     2                    | ..---                                  |                   7                    | --...
                     3                    | ...--                                  |                   8                    | ---..
                     4                    | ....-                                  |                   9                    | ----.
                     5                    | .....                                  |                   0                    | -----
  ──────
  ### Step 4: Format into the Flag

  In picoCTF, audio Morse challenges (such as morse-code) typically follow one of these formats:

  1. Convert the decoded message to all lowercase, replacing spaces with underscores:
    picoCTF{wh47_h47h_90d_wr0u9h7}

  2. Or keep standard uppercase letters as decoded:
    picoCTF{WH47_H47H_90D_WR0U9H7}

  (Check the challenge prompt for whether lowercase/uppercase is specified).

